NAME
     gzip - compress and uncompress

SYNOPSIS
     gzip [-d] [-c] [-1..-9] [FILE...]
     gunzip [-c] [FILE...]
     zcat [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     gzip compresses each FILE to FILE.gz and removes the original;
     gunzip does the reverse. Called as zcat it writes the uncompressed
     bytes to standard output and leaves the file alone.

OPTIONS
     -d        uncompress
     -c        to standard output, keeping the original
     -1..-9    how hard to try

SEE ALSO
     tar(1), cat(1)
